<title>ITALY: Italian majority to discuss DPEF plan on Monday.</title>
<headline>Italian majority to discuss DPEF plan on Monday.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The leaders of the parties that make up Italy's centre-left coalition will meet on Monday to discuss the government's annual document of three-year rolling economic targets (DPEF), political sources said on Saturday.</p>
<p>They gave no further details.</p>
<p>Regional affairs minister Franco Bassanini said on Friday that the document, expected to provide outlines of key welfare reforms and targets to form the basis for Italy's plan to join the single European currency, would be passed by the cabinet by the end of next week.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2505</p>
</text>
